{"cwd": "/sandbox/runs/harbor-dispatch/runs/train-INC-63-r2/harbor-dispatch", "isSidechain": false, "message": {"content": [{"content": "INC-63  Port codes typed with a space or hyphen are not recognised\nstatus: open   priority: P3   area: ports   reported: 2026-07-06 by customer-service\n\nAgents copy port codes out of booking emails, where they are usually written with a\nspace or a hyphen between the country and the location, and the lookup then says the\nport does not exist. Rotterdam written as NL RTM or nl-rtm should resolve exactly like\nNLRTM.\n\nAcceptance:\n  normaliseLocode removes spaces and hyphens as well as normalising case, so\n  normaliseLocode(\"nl-rtm\") and normaliseLocode(\"NL RTM\") both return \"NLRTM\" and\n  portByCode(\"NL RTM\") finds Rotterdam.\n\nFiles:\n  src/ports/locode.ts", "is_error": false, "tool_use_id": "toolu_01JgTJJ11pvwQthHf89bLBK5", "type": "tool_result"}], "role": "user"}, "sessionId": "0505ea57-e719-40a6-829b-d734a0088e47", "timestamp": "2026-09-28T03:35:40.235Z", "toolUseResult": {"stdout": "INC-63  Port codes typed with a space or hyphen are not recognised\nstatus: open   priority: P3   area: ports   reported: 2026-07-06 by customer-service\n\nAgents copy port codes out of booking emails, where they are usually written with a\nspace or a hyphen between the country and the location, and the lookup then says the\nport does not exist. Rotterdam written as NL RTM or nl-rtm should resolve exactly like\nNLRTM.\n\nAcceptance:\n  normaliseLocode removes spaces and hyphens as well as normalising case, so\n  normaliseLocode(\"nl-rtm\") and normaliseLocode(\"NL RTM\") both return \"NLRTM\" and\n  portByCode(\"NL RTM\") finds Rotterdam.\n\nFiles:\n  src/ports/locode.ts"}, "type": "user"}
